d stores, as well as through online and internet-enabled mobile devices. The company was founded in 1994 and is headquartered in Miami, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert  Lisy | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 67 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $555K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 12%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $14K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["International Money Express, In is a micro-cap technology business with a $190M market cap on $608M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 50% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 42-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $16M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.13\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 4.7\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 8.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 8.1% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 30% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading at a 57% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 83% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Technology peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (IMXI) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/101/The_Technical_Signals_Behind_IMXI_That_Institutions_Follow_111126115401_1794459241.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794459241.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[